# The frontend needs NO configuration for a normal deployment.
#
# In production Laravel serves the built app from its own public/ directory, so
# the API is same-origin and src/lib/config.js uses relative URLs like
# `/api/health`. Leave VITE_API_BASE_URL unset and it stays that way.
#
# In development it defaults to http://localhost:8000 automatically.
#
# Only set this if your API lives somewhere else — and if you do, put it in
# `.env.development`, NOT `.env`. Vite loads `.env` in every mode, so a value
# there would be compiled into the production bundle and the deployed site would
# call localhost.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
